        { "text": "$1 - \\frac{5}{x + 3}$", "why": "Made $b$ negative by computing $3 - 8$ instead of $8 - 3$." },
        { "text": "$1 + \\frac{8}{x + 3}$", "why": "Left the numerator constant as $8$ without subtracting the $a(x + 3)$ part." },
        { "text": "$8 + \\frac{5}{x + 3}$", "why": "Put the numerator constant $8$ in place of $a$ instead of $1$." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$\\frac{x + 8}{x + 3} = a + \\frac{b}{x + 3}$\n$x + 8 = a(x + 3) + b$\n$a = 1$ and $3a + b = 8$\n$b = 5$\n$\\frac{x + 8}{x + 3} = 1 + \\frac{5}{x + 3}$"
