      "solution_text": "$\\frac{12}{(x - 2)(x + 4)} = \\frac{A}{x - 2} + \\frac{B}{x + 4}$\n$12 = A(x + 4) + B(x - 2)$\nLet $x = 2$: $12 = 6A$, so $A = 2$\nLet $x = -4$: $12 = -6B$, so $B = -2$\n$\\frac{12}{(x - 2)(x + 4)} = \\frac{2}{x - 2} - \\frac{2}{x + 4}$"
